From 11252f95042f827fbb74a3258eff6ab4b867d80d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 00:43:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vr: expose Steam Frame controllers to WebXR

Add the /interaction_profiles/valve/frame_controller_valve OpenXR
interaction profile, reported to pages as "valve-frame" with a
"generic-trigger-squeeze-thumbstick" fallback.

The Frame splits a full gamepad across two controllers: A/B/X/Y and a
menu button on the right, a D-pad and a view button on the left, and a
bumper, grip, trigger and thumbstick on both. Without a Frame profile
SteamVR remaps the controllers onto the Index profile, which exposes A
and B only, so X/Y, the D-pad, the bumpers, view and menu are lost.

Gamepad layout (xr-standard, then fixed Frame slots so the indices do
not shift when a component is unbound):
  0 trigger, 1 squeeze, 2 touchpad placeholder, 3 thumbstick
  right: 4 A, 5 B, 6 X, 7 Y, 8 bumper, 9 menu
  left:  4 D-pad up, 5 down, 6 left, 7 right, 8 bumper, 9 view

The Frame menu button gets its own button type (kAppMenu) instead of
kMenu, which OpenXRInputHelper treats as the exit gesture; on the Frame
the system button and SteamVR dashboard already end a session.

The Frame's component paths are not publicly documented, and runtimes
that predate the Frame do not know the profile. Every other profile's
bindings remain fatal, but a rejected Frame suggestion is retried with
the paths that mirror the Index controller, and then skipped, so input
keeps working through the runtime's remapping.

Bug: none
Test: device_unittests --gtest_filter='OpenXrInteractionProfilesTest.*'
